<title>USA: Top manufacturing cities - survey.</title>
<headline>Top manufacturing cities - survey.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the 22 cities with the most major manufacturing companies in 1996, according to IndustryWeek magazine's IndustryWeek 1000 list, compiled with Dun &amp; Bradstreet Corp. and Moody's Investor Service.</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>Tokyo		  - 143 companies</p>
<p>London		 -  50</p>
<p>Osaka, Japan	 -  26</p>
<p>New York	     -  19</p>
<p>Seoul, South Korea -  16</p>
<p>Chicago		-  14</p>
<p>Paris		  -  14</p>
<p>Houston		-  11</p>
<p>Stockholm, Sweden  -  11</p>
<p>Helsinki, Finland  -  10</p>
<p>Toronto		-  10</p>
<p>Pittsburgh	   -   9</p>
<p>Kyoto, Japan	 -   8</p>
<p>Brussels, Belgium  -   7</p>
<p>Cleveland	    -   7</p>
<p>Johannesburg	 -   7</p>
<p>Montreal	     -   7</p>
<p>St. Louis	    -   7</p>
<p>Dallas		 -   6</p>
<p>Milan		  -   6</p>
<p>Stamford, Conn.    -   6</p>
<p>Sydney, Australia  -   6</p>
</text>
